    "['trust upstream default', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface <interface-name> transport-preference ip', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ldp interface <interface-name> transport-preference ip\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `trust upstream default` command indicates that LDP should prefer IP forwarding for its control packets (rather than using MPLS paths). In Juniper, the equivalent is setting the transport preference to IP for LDP on the interface.\\n\\nNote: `<interface-name>` should be replaced with the actual Juniper interface name (e.g., ge-0/0/0). The exact interface naming wasn't provided in the Huawei config, so I used a placeholder.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface <interface-name> transport-preference ip'}]]": 1,
    "['trust upstream default', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/0 transport-preference ipv4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/0 transport-preference ipv4\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-2/0/0 transport-preference ipv4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `trust upstream default` command indicates that LDP should prefer IPv4 transport for establishing LDP sessions. In Juniper, the equivalent is achieved by setting `transport-preference ipv4` under the LDP interface configuration. Since the command was applied to both interfaces in the Huawei configuration, both Juniper interface configurations are included.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/0 transport-preference ipv4'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-2/0/0 transport-preference ipv4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/0 transport-preference ipv4\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-2/0/0 transport-preference ipv4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `trust upstream default` command indicates that LDP should prefer IPv4 transport for establishing LDP sessions. In Juniper, the equivalent is achieved by setting `transport-preference ipv4` under the LDP interface configuration. Since the command was applied to both interfaces in the Huawei configuration, both Juniper interface configurations are included.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-2/0/0 transport-preference ipv4'}]]": 1,
